## 1. MISSION & NON-NEGOTIABLES

Build **Clinicalc**: an offline-first Android app that gives clinicians and students fast, correct, beautifully rendered access to 300+ medical scoring systems, bedside calculators and unit converters — wrapped in a UI that reproduces the **behaviour and feel** of Apple's iOS 26 "Liquid Glass" as faithfully as Android's graphics stack allows.

| # | Non-negotiable | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| N1 | Correctness beats beauty | A beautiful wrong number is the highest-severity defect in this project. |
| N2 | Glass is chrome, content is solid | Glass floats *above* content (nav, toolbars, controls, sheets). Results, inputs, formulas and reference text sit on solid surfaces. This is also Apple's own rule for the material. |
| N3 | Legibility floor | Every input and result meets the contrast targets in §4.5 against the **worst-case backdrop**, in every glass mode. |
| N4 | Graceful degradation | Same layout and flows on every device; fewer effects on weaker ones. Never a broken, janky or unreadable screen. |
| N5 | Original assets only | No SF Pro, no SF Symbols, no Apple marks or screenshots, no "iOS" branding. Replicate *behaviour*, not assets. |
| N6 | Every number is traceable | Each tool shows formula, source citation, confidence and copyright status. |
| N7 | No code-from-data | Formulas are declarative and run by a safe evaluator. No `eval`, no script strings in JSON. |

