## 4. LIQUID GLASS SPECIFICATION

Reference for *behaviour* (not assets): Apple's WWDC25 session "Meet Liquid Glass" (#219) and the HIG "Materials" section.

### 4.1 Principle → Android implementation

| Apple behaviour | What it must feel like | Android implementation | Fallback (lower tier) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Real-time lensing** | Content behind glass bends near the edges; the centre stays readable. Not a flat frosted plane. | Record the scrolling content once into a shared `GraphicsLayer` per screen. Glass samples it through a `RenderEffect` chain: blur (API 31+) → AGSL `RuntimeShader` lens (API 33+). Lens = **rounded-rect / capsule SDF**; refraction displaces samples along the SDF gradient inside an edge band ("compressed rim"); tiny per-channel offset for dispersion; +10–30% saturation on the sampled backdrop (vibrancy); fine noise grain against banding. | Blur + tint + rim highlight (no refraction) → translucent gradient + rim → solid. |
| **Specular highlights** | A moving sheen on the rim that reacts to tilt and touch. | Fresnel-style rim highlight in the shader; light direction driven by `TYPE_GAME_ROTATION_VECTOR` (or gravity) through a low-pass filter, ≤30 Hz. Unregister sensors when paused/static. | Fixed light from top-left (~315°). |
| **Organic materialisation** | Elements appear/disappear by *modulating light bending*, not by alpha fade. | Animate lens strength, blur radius, rim intensity and shadow together (0 → 1). Opacity stays ~1 during the animation. | Short scale + alpha crossfade. |
| **Thickening on expand** | When a toolbar becomes a menu or sheet, the material gets *thicker*: deeper shadow, softer light scatter. | Interpolate between material tiers (§4.3) — Regular → Thick — for blur, shadow radius/alpha, and refraction strength during the expand spring. | Interpolate shadow + tint only. |
| **Fluid morphing** | Nearby glass shapes merge like liquid; a button grows into its menu. | `GlassContainer` renders adjacent shapes in **one pass** using an SDF **smooth-union**. Cap shapes per container (start at 8). Morph bounds with a spring. | Shared-element bounds transform. |
| **Interactive glass** | Press = the glass swells, brightens, springs back. Dragging the tab indicator = a magnifying lens sliding between tabs. | Press: scale ≈ 1.04–1.08 + rim boost, spring release (start `damping 0.7, stiffness ≈ 380`). Tab indicator: draggable lens with ~1.1× magnification while touched. | Scale + tint change. |
| **Intelligent legibility** | Foreground flips light/dark based on what's under it. | §4.5. | Theme-driven foreground + guaranteed scrim. |
| **Concentricity** | Shapes nest and echo the screen's corners. Capsules everywhere. | Nested radius rule: `inner = outer − padding`. Read device corners via `WindowInsets.getRoundedCorner` (API 31+) and align edge-hugging bars to them. Implement a **continuous-corner (squircle)** shape, not a plain rounded rect. Default control shape = capsule. | Fixed 28 dp outer radius. |
| **Shrinking chrome** | Bottom bar collapses out of the way on scroll-down, returns on scroll-up. | `NestedScrollConnection` drives a `collapseFraction` (0–1). Collapsed = compact capsule showing only the active tab; the lens morphs, not fades. | Slide + alpha. |
| **Layered icon** | Depth from stacked translucent layers. | Adaptive icon: foreground / background / **monochrome** (themed) layers, designed with layered depth. (The launcher can't composite real glass — fake it in the artwork.) | — |
| **User adjustability** | Clear ↔ Tinted control for legibility. | §4.7 Glass Style setting. | — |

### 4.2 Where glass is allowed

| Surface | Glass? | Material |
|---|---|---|
| Bottom navigation bar, top app bar / search capsule | ✅ | Regular |
| Floating action cluster, filter chips, segmented controls, toggles, sliders' thumbs | ✅ | Thin / Regular |
| Bottom sheets & menus (chrome + container) | ✅ | Thick |
| Toasts / snackbars | ✅ | Thin |
| Score input fields, steppers' value areas | ❌ | Solid tonal surface |
| **Result value, risk band, interpretation text** | ❌ (glass *rim* only) | Solid + rim light |
| Formula, citations, limitations, long text, tables | ❌ | Solid |
| Ads | ❌ | Never on glass |
| Glass on glass (stacked) | ❌ | Forbidden — flatten the lower layer |

### 4.3 Material tiers — **starting values, tune on-device in the Glass Lab**

| Tier | Use | Blur (dp) | Tint α (light / dark) | Edge band (dp) | Refraction (0–1) | Dispersion (0–1) | Shadow |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Thin | chips, tags, toasts | 6 | .10 / .08 | 10 | .45 | 0 | soft, small |
| Regular | bars, buttons, segmented | 16 | .14 / .10 | 16 | .60 | .15 | soft |
| Thick | sheets, morphing menus, result "condense" | 28 | .22 / .16 | 22 | .80 | .20 | deep, wide |
| Solid | a11y mode, Tier S, all content | 0 | tonal surface | — | 0 | 0 | 1 px inner highlight |

### 4.4 Ambient backdrop (needed — glass over flat white/black looks dead)

- A slowly drifting, very low-contrast **mesh-gradient layer** behind the content gives glass something to refract. Muted "Calm Interface" hues; **per-specialty hue shift** (e.g., cardio, neuro, renal each get a desaturated identity hue).
- In true-black OLED dark mode the ambient layer is sparse and dim (a few soft glows), so blacks stay black while glass still has material.
- Ambient layer animates only when the screen is idle-visible; pauses under battery saver, Tier ≥ C, or animator scale = 0.

### 4.5 Adaptive legibility (the hard part)

| Requirement | Target |
|---|---|
| Body / input text | ≥ 4.5 : 1 (WCAG 2.2 AA) |
| Large text, icons | ≥ 3 : 1 |
| **Result value & risk label** | **aim ≥ 7 : 1** |
| Font scale | works to 200% without clipping; capsules grow |
| Tap targets | ≥ 48 dp; capsule height 48–56 dp |
| Risk tier | never colour alone — colour + icon + text label |

**Method (deterministic first):**
1. Guarantee contrast with tint + an adaptive scrim so a single theme-chosen foreground works. Prefer this — it costs nothing per frame.
2. Only where the backdrop can genuinely swing light↔dark under a control (e.g., scrolling bento cards under the bottom bar), sample backdrop luminance from a downscaled region (≈16×16) at ≤10 Hz, with **hysteresis** (~0.05) and a 150 ms foreground crossfade. Measure the cost; drop to method 1 if it shows in frame time.
3. **CI check:** render every glass component over worst-case backdrops — pure white, pure black, max-chroma stripes, high-frequency checkerboard, each risk-tier bento colour — and assert the contrast ratios above. Run on an API 33+ emulator or device (JVM-only tests can't run AGSL).

### 4.6 Device tiers, budgets, fallbacks

| Tier | Condition (auto-detected) | Experience |
|---|---|---|
| **A** | API 33+, capable GPU, no thermal throttling | Full: refraction, dispersion, sensor specular, morph |
| **B** | API 31–32, or mid GPU | Blur + tint + static specular; no refraction |
| **C** | API < 31, low RAM, or sustained jank | Translucent gradient + rim; no backdrop sampling |
| **S** | Battery saver, user "Solid", accessibility | Solid tonal surfaces; keeps the same layout |

Rules:
- **One shared backdrop layer per screen.** Never one per element.
- **≤ 4 simultaneous backdrop-sampling glass elements** on screen (start value; measure). Bottom bar + top bar + 1–2 floating.
- **No real glass inside `LazyColumn` items.** List items use pre-baked "glass-look" surfaces without sampling.
- Render the blur at reduced scale (≈0.5×) where quality allows.
- **Runtime governor:** watch frame stats (JankStats); on sustained jank step down one tier and remember the decision per device.
- Sensors off when the screen is static, in battery saver, or animator scale = 0. Everything motion-related honours `ANIMATOR_DURATION_SCALE`.
- Targets: no visible jank while scrolling with glass on; p95 frame time within the display's refresh budget on the **physical low-end reference device**. Emulator numbers don't count as evidence.

