## 9. ANTI-PATTERNS (reject on sight)

- "Glass" = white at 20% alpha over a flat background. That's frosted plastic, not lensing.
- Blurring every list row, or a backdrop layer per element.
- Glass on glass; text over a busy backdrop with no scrim.
- Putting a result value, band, or formula on a refracting surface.
- Alpha-fading glass in and out instead of modulating lens/blur/rim.
- Hardcoded per-score screens; string `eval`; formulas copied from memory instead of the source files.
- Hiding low-confidence or restricted tools rather than labelling or gating them.
- Padding the tool count.
- Apple fonts, SF Symbols or Apple screenshots.
- Dark glass on pure black with no ambient material (looks dead).
- Shipping effects that haven't been measured on a low-end physical device.

